"""Float VALU forms with clamp/omod/op_sel/neg the game's shaders use, against words an RDNA2 GPU returned (no model).

Every row was run natively on an AMD Radeon RDNA2 iGPU (gfx1036, Ryzen 9 9950X3D, Windows AMD driver 32.0.21045.16010)
through tools/hw_oracle with AMD clang 23 (rocm-sdk-core 10.0.0), in the MODE inferred for the game (IEEE 0,
DX10_CLAMP 1, f32 denormals flushed, f16 denormals kept). v1..v3 hold the operands, v4 starts as 0xDEADBEEF (v_fmac
and v_fma_mixlo/hi start from v3, which they read or partly keep), and the word in v4 after the lines is the expected
one. An SGPR operand is set with s_mov_b32 first; a literal is one of three fixed words.

The forms are the 542 distinct float VALU forms that carry clamp, an omod, op_sel/op_sel_hi or neg/abs in the
26,503 listings of the 1.0.2.1 package (opcode, operand kinds, inline constants, modifiers), up to 120 random
operand triples each. Only the form is taken from the game; every word here is synthetic. The 1,616 rows are a
sample, up to three per form with distinct results. The measured cases not listed match too, except for differences
already on record: an omod turning a -0 result into +0 (docs/design.md, Output modifiers rows; #1281), f32 denormal
operands or intermediate results (SHADER-377), NaN sign/payload, 1-ulp differences in v_rcp/v_log/v_sin, and cases
whose translation is undefined in SPIR-V (FClamp of a NaN, the root or log of a negative or zero).
"""
